The file contains information that is used by various routines to
initialize  and  control the use of terminal special files.  This
information is read with the library routines.  There is one line
in the file per special device file.   Fields  are  separated  by
tabs  and/or spaces.  Fields comprising more than one word should
be enclosed in double quotes (‘‘"’’).  Blank lines  and  comments
may  appear  anywhere in the file; comments are delimited by hash
marks (‘‘#’’) and new lines.  Any unspecified fields will default
to null.  Each line in has the format: The  first  field  is  the
name  of  the  terminal special file as it is found in The second
field of the file is the command to execute for the line, usually
which initializes and opens the line, setting the speed,  waiting
for  a  user  name and executing the program.  However, it can be
any desired command, for example the start up for a window system
terminal emulator or some other daemon process, and  can  contain
multiple  words if quoted.  The third field is the type of termi‐
nal usually connected to that tty line, normally the one found in
the data base file.  The environment variable is initialized with
the value by either or The remaining fields set flags in the  en‐
try  (see  or  specify a window system process that will maintain
